Do you really think so? It will give you gold or a gem or a ring or an
amulet every one thousand turns. After 20000 turns, you have 20 items,
10 of them being just gold or gems, assuming equal probability for the
four types of items (I suppose, one would normally make amulets a bit
rarer, so I may even underestimate this here). So you would have about
five rings and five amulets. To find five rings in 20000 turns by
exploring the dungeon instead (and being unburdened) is not that
uncommon. So all it would be useful for would be the amulets. But you
*might* get two amulets of restful sleep and two of strangulation,
leaving you with one possibly useful one. And if you invoke the thing
too early, it will ignore you and your timeout will increase.

If I had an early wish, I would certainly prefer to spend it on some
item increasing my chances of survival, i.e. armor or a good weapon. The
chest would decrease these chances for quite some time (likely making
you burdened), all for a doubtful benefit. (Of course, you might get an
amulet of life saving on the first invocation...) It might be acceptable
for an 18+ strength character, but for such a role wishing for good
armor (GDSM) will almost directly promote him into the class of
ascendable characters, which the chest will not do.


